{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>The first time</b><br>That flowed down. Some say [it is from] the Aramaic translation קרח (it means גלוש), but this is far-fetched in meaning. Some say the lamed is superfluous. The correct view in my eyes is that it has no parallel, and its meaning is: they slipped and descended." "<b>The second time</b><br>עדר העזים [a flock of goats]: when it is on a mountain, one appears above another." "<b>The third time</b><br>The Shekhinah praises Kneset Israel and says: הנך יפה רעיתי [Behold, you are beautiful, my friend]." "עיניך יונים [Your eyes are doves]. These are the prophets." "שערך [Your hair]. These are the Nazirites, for they grow hair."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The bracketed material in the Hebrew suggests textual corruption; the phrase גלוש והוא רחוק בענין appears to be a gloss. Transmitted hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:13.545964501Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}